-- Test file for the promotion of section-level facts to API inputs in
-- jl4-service. When @export functions read a fact declared once for the
-- section (a section GIVEN; a module-level ASSUME until 2026-09-06, promoted
-- the same way), that fact is exposed as an API input parameter.

§ `Environment`
    GIVEN temperature IS A NUMBER  -- simple values become API params
          humidity IS A NUMBER
          `is authorized` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO BOOLEAN  -- function-typed ones are skipped (per design decision)

-- Test 1: Simple function referencing one section-level fact
-- Expected: API exposes `temperature` as input parameter
@export default Is the temperature warm?
`is warm` MEANS temperature > 25

-- Test 2: Function referencing several section-level facts
-- Expected: API exposes both `temperature` and `humidity`
@export Is the environment comfortable?
`is comfortable` MEANS
  temperature > 18 AND temperature < 26 AND humidity < 70

-- Test 3: Function with its own GIVEN plus a section-level fact
-- Expected: API exposes `threshold` (rule GIVEN) and `temperature` (section GIVEN)
@export Does temperature exceed threshold?
GIVEN threshold IS A NUMBER
`exceeds threshold` threshold MEANS temperature > threshold

-- Test 4: Referencing a function-typed section-level fact from an @export is
-- rejected at typecheck — it can't be evaluated (it stays as an assumed
-- term), so the exported function would fail at runtime.
-- We therefore call the predicate only from a non-exported helper, and
-- the exported wrapper just returns TRUE for the schema test.
`check auth` MEANS `is authorized` 42

@export Check authorization status
`exported auth check` MEANS TRUE
